O .claude/rules/backend/architecture-style.md 30-30 NN - ARC-005,ARC-013 | they are the natural repository-boundary candidates | Considered as a hidden repository-per-aggregate rule. Rejected: the sentence is descriptive ('natural candidates'), conditional on an already approved DDD design, and imposes no obligation or prohibition. | none
O .claude/rules/backend/architecture-style.md 28-28 PL R35 ARC-004 | unless the approved specification already requires them | Suspected relaxation EXTRA (approval waived when the specification requires DDD). Kept oracle-linked: an approved specification is itself an approval of the required behavior (GOV-001), so ARC-004's approval requirement is satisfied rather than relaxed. | Rich-domain patterns demanded by the approved specification need no separate approval.
O .claude/rules/backend/dependencies.md 12-12 PL R54 DEP-006 | a `VersionOverride` needs a recorded reason | Suspected EXTRA (recorded reason for VersionOverride). Kept oracle-linked: DEP-006 says PackageReference entries are 'normally' versionless; requiring a reason for the exceptional override specifies the 'normally' qualifier without forbidding any oracle-permitted outcome. | A VersionOverride without a stated reason is non-conformant.
O .claude/rules/backend-tests/test-framework.md 10-10 PL R100 TST-001,RUN-009 | In an established project that deliberately uses another framework, follow that convention | Suspected relaxation EXTRA. Kept oracle-linked: TST-001 is a DEFAULT and RUN-009 makes repository conventions authoritative, so following a deliberately chosen existing framework is within the oracle. | In a project already using xUnit deliberately, xUnit continues to be used.
O .claude/rules/frontend/dependencies.md 10-10 PL R125 DEP-007,WF-018 | `package.json` and `package-lock.json` must be committed and kept consistent | Suspected EXTRA (lockfile must be committed). Kept oracle-linked: DEP-007 requires a consistent package-lock and WF-018 presumes a maintained lockfile; 'committed' means version-controlled, not an instruction to run git commit (GOV-015 still governs commits). | The lockfile is kept under source control.
O .claude/rules/common/security.md 22-22 PL R118 SEC-007 | application-level HTTP-to-HTTPS redirection is not required | Suspected relaxation EXTRA. Kept oracle-linked: SEC-007 itself requires respecting the actual hosting topology; waiving app-level redirection where the deployment provides the secure boundary is that same qualifier. | App-level HTTPS redirection may be omitted behind TLS-terminating infrastructure.
O .claude/MAP.md 11-11 PL R285 GOV-001,GOV-003,GOV-017 | product inputs never override policy | Initially registered as LINK_UNCERTAIN (does policy outrank an approved specification, restricting GOV-001?). Resolved after reading the always-loaded owner CLAUDE.md line 24: inputs 'may request a decision change' but 'must not silently override engineering policy or recorded decisions', and CLAUDE.md line 30 classifies what the specification already requires as Decided. That is GOV-017 decision control, not a restriction of GOV-001; the map's unqualified 'never' is a not-loaded summary with no separate runtime effect. | A specification or task that conflicts with a recorded decision triggers a Decision Request instead of a silent override.
